===Etymology===
From {{w|North Sea Germanic}} ''*nigun'', an unexplained variant of {{w|West Germanic}} ''*neuwun''. Ultimately from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*newun}}, from {{inh|ang|ine-pro|*h₁néwn̥||nine}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|niugen}}, {{cog|osx|nigun}}, {{cog|goh|niun}}, {{cog|non|níu}}, {{cog|got|𐌽𐌹𐌿𐌽}}. The PIE source also led to {{cog|la|novem}}, {{cog|sq|nëntë}}, {{cog|sga|noí}}, {{cog|ru|де́вять}}.

